\ Install - Information                                                                                                         This is the source to the DX-Forth installer program.                                                                           INSTALL customises the DX-Forth compiler and turnkey            applications for a variety of video terminals.  Also,           the CPU speed, terminal delay times, arrow key codes            and no-warmboot option may be adjusted.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ Load block                                                    empty  forth definitions  decimal                               application                                                                                                                     : TITLE ( -- )  ." DX-INSTALL 1.5" cr ;                                                                                         cr .( loading ) title  2 #screens 1- thru                                                                                       cr .( Save to disk? ) y/n [if]                                    turnkey install INSTALL                                       [then]                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \ ZINS                                                          1 fload ZINS.SCR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ CLS EMITS +PLACE ?PLACE CHANGE? .HB .ONOFF                    : CLS ( -- )  30 0 do cr loop ;  \ simple clear screen                                                                          : EMITS ( n char -- )  swap 0 ?do dup emit loop drop ;                                                                          : +PLACE ( a u a2 -- )  count +string swap 1- c! ;                                                                              : ?PLACE ( a u a2 -- )  over if place end  drop 2drop ;                                                                         : CHANGE? ( -- f )  ."  Change? " y/n ;                                                                                         : .HB ( u -- )  hex  s>d <# # # #> type space  decimal ;                                                                        : .ONOFF ( flag -- )  if ." ON " end  ." OFF " ;                                                                                                                                                \ cf !FNAME @FNAME HANDLE IN-FILE DTA-FILE                      here value cf ( -- a )  \ current file handle                                                                                   -? : HANDLE  create  max-path 1+ cell+ allot  does> to cf ;                                                                     : !FNAME ( a n -- )  max-path min  cf cell+ place ;             : @FNAME ( -- a n )  cf cell+ count ;                                                                                           \ File handles                                                  handle IN-FILE   handle DTA-FILE                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ HELP FERR FOPEN FCREAT FREAD FWRITE FSEEK FCLOSE              \ Show help and exit                                            : HELP ( -- )                                                     cr ." Installer for DX-Forth and compiled applications." cr     cr ." Use: INSTALL filename[.com] [termfile[.dta]]"  abort ;                                                                  \ Encountered file error, display msg, filename then quit       : FERR ( ? ior a u -- ? )  rot 0= if  2drop  end                  cr ." File error: "  type  ."  - "  @fname type  abort ;                                                                      : FOPEN  ( a n fam -- )  open-file  s" open"  ferr  cf ! ;      : FCREAT ( a n fam -- )  create-file  s" create"  ferr  cf ! ;  : FREAD  ( a n -- n' )  cf @ read-file  s" read"  ferr ;        : FWRITE ( a n -- )  cf @ write-file  s" write"  ferr ;         : FSEEK  ( ud -- )  cf @ reposition-file  s" position"  ferr ;  : FCLOSE ( -- )  cf @ close-file  s" close"  ferr ;             \ ARG                                                           \ Parse the CP/M command line for the n'th blank delimited      \ parameter.  Return the address and length and a true flag if  \ found, otherwise return false.                                : ARG ( n -- adr len -1 | 0 )                                     >r  0 0  cmdtail  r> 0 ?do                                        2nip                                                            bl skip  2dup bl scan                                           rot over - -rot                                               loop 2drop                                                      dup if  -1  end  and ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ Program constants                                             0    value    #TERMS    \ number of terminals in DTA file       0    value    TERM      \ working terminal#                     $95  constant TLEN      \ length of each term definition        $100 constant CHUNK     \ in-file chunk to get                  20   constant ISIZ      \ size input buffer / terminal name     200  constant TMAX      \ max #terminals                                                                                        \ Storage areas allocated at run-time                           here value IN-BASE  ( -- a )  \ in-file                         here value DTA-BASE ( -- a )  \ dta-file                        here value TBUF     ( -- a )  \ temp terminal buffer            here value SBUF     ( -- a )  \ swap/work buffer                here value IBUF     ( -- a )  \ console input                   here value XBUF     ( -- a )  \ terminal index                                                                                  \ >TARGET ENTER                                                 \ Convert logical adr to target adr                             : >TARGET ( a -- a' )  $100 - in-base + ;                                                                                       \ Get input from console                                        : ENTER ( -- adr len )  ibuf dup isiz accept ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ 0TERM DTA-END >DTA DBUF NAME                                  \ First terminal in DTA                                         : 0TERM ( -- a )  dta-base 2 cells + ;                                                                                          \ DTA end + 1                                                   : DTA-END ( -- a )  0term  #terms tlen * + ;                                                                                    \ Get adr of terminal n                                         : >DTA ( n -- a )  cells xbuf + @ ;                                                                                             \ Get adr of selected terminal                                  : DBUF ( -- a )  term >dta ;                                                                                                    \ Get name of terminal n                                        : NAME ( n -- adr len )  >dta count ;                                                                                           \ SET.S SET.W SET.B                                             \ Install terminal data at offs to target at adr                : SET.S ( a ofs -- )  dbuf +  count rot  >target place ;        : SET.W ( a ofs -- )  dbuf +  @ swap  >target ! ;               : SET.B ( a ofs -- )  dbuf +  c@ swap  >target c! ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \ TNAME TINIT TEXIT TCM TBIN TPOS TOFFS TDCM TCLS               hex                                                             : TNAME ( -- ) 153  0 set.s ;  \ terminal name                  : TINIT ( -- ) 16B 16 set.s ;  \ term init                      : TEXIT ( -- ) 17B 26 set.s ;  \ term exit                      : TCM   ( -- ) 18B 36 set.s ;  \ cursor motion template         : TBIN  ( -- ) 19B 46 set.b ;  \ binary mode                    : TPOS  ( -- ) 19E 47 set.w ;  \ col row pos                    : TOFFS ( -- ) 19C 49 set.w ;  \ col row offset                 : TDCM  ( -- ) 1A0 4B set.w ;  \ cm delay                       : TCLS  ( -- ) 1A2 4D set.s ;  \ clear screen                   decimal                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ THOM TDCLS THIL TNOR TDEOL TEOL TINS TDEL TCR                 hex                                                             : THOM  ( -- ) 1A8 53 set.s ;  \ home cursor                    : TDCLS ( -- ) 1BA 59 set.w ;  \ cls delay                      : THIL  ( -- ) 1C2 5B set.s ;  \ hilight video                  : TNOR  ( -- ) 1C8 61 set.s ;  \ normal video                   : TDEOL ( -- ) 1CE 67 set.w ;  \ eol delay                      : TEOL  ( -- ) 1BC 69 set.s ;  \ clear to end-of-line           : TINS  ( -- ) 1AE 6F set.s ;  \ insert line                    : TDEL  ( -- ) 1B4 75 set.s ;  \ delete line                    : TCR   ( -- ) 168 7B set.w ;  \ # cols rows                    decimal                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ ZDATA SWAP-OUT SWAP-IN ZINSTALL                               \ ZINS data area excluding speed                                $14F $200 over - 2constant ZDATA ( -- a u )                                                                                     : SWAP-OUT ( -- )                                                 sbuf  $124 @ over !  cell+ zdata rot swap cmove ;                                                                             : SWAP-IN ( -- )                                                  sbuf  dup @ $124 !  cell+ zdata cmove ;                                                                                       : ZINSTALL ( -- )                                                 swap-out                          \ save existing               zins                              \ install from Termcap        $124  dup @  swap >target !       \ move speed                  zdata  $14F >target  swap cmove   \ move zdata                  swap-in ;                         \ restore existing          \ OPEN-TARGET                                                   \ Read first chunk of target file into memory                   : OPEN-TARGET ( -- )                                              in-file                               \ select filehandle       1 arg  0= if help then                \ get first filename      s" COM" +ext  !fname                  \ append filetype         @fname r/w fopen                      \ open target file        chunk reserve to in-base              \ allot buffer            in-base chunk fread ( u)              \ read target file        chunk -                               \ check size              $111 >target @ $4683 -  or            \ check DX-Forth id.      s" not a DX-Forth application"  ferr ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ READ-DTA                                                      \ Read DTA file into memory                                     : READ-DTA ( -- )                                                 dta-file                              \ select filehandle       2 arg                                 \ if second filename      if    s" DTA" +ext                    \ append filetype         else  s" INSTALL.DTA"  then  !fname   \ else use default        @fname r/w fopen                      \ open DTA file           pad 256 + to dta-base                 \ assign buffer           dta-base unused fread drop            \ read DTA file           fclose                                \ close                   dta-base  dup @ to #terms             \ get #terminals          cell+ @  tlen -                       \ check DTA id.           s" not a TPascal terminal file"  ferr ;                                                                                                                                                       \ CLOSE-TARGET SAVE-TARGET ALTERED SAVE-DTA                     : CLOSE-TARGET ( -- )  in-file  fclose ;                                                                                        : SAVE-TARGET ( -- )  \ update target file                        in-file  0. fseek  in-base chunk fwrite ;                                                                                     variable ALTERED  \ DTA changed                                                                                                 : SAVE-DTA ( -- )  \ overwrite DTA file                           altered @ if                                                      dta-file  @fname r/w fcreat                                     dta-base 2 cells fwrite ( hdr)                                  xbuf  #terms 0 ?do  dup @ tlen fwrite  cell+  loop drop         fclose                                                        then ;                                                                                                                        \ SORT $COMP                                                    \ Bubblesort addr/cells                                         defer PRECEDES ( x1 x2 -- f )  \ comparison                                                                                     : SORT ( adr siz -- )                                             begin dup while 1-                                                2dup cells bounds ?do                                             i 2@ precedes if  i 2@ swap i 2!  altered on  then            1 cells +loop                                                 repeat 2drop ;                                                                                                                \ Compare counted strings                                       : $COMP ( a1 a2 -- -1|0|1 )                                       >r  count  r> count  caps compare ;                                                                                           :noname $comp 0< ; is precedes                                  \ SORT-TERMS CATALOG                                            \ Sort terminals by name                                        : SORT-TERMS ( -- )  xbuf #terms sort ;                                                                                         \ Index & sort terminals                                        : CATALOG ( -- )                                                  #terms tmax > if  cr ." Too many terminals" abort  then         xbuf  dta-end 0term  ?do  i over !  cell+  tlen +loop           sort-terms ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ #SELECT SELECT ANYKEY INVALID                                 \ Select number in range n1 to n2.  Return n3 true | false      : #SELECT ( n1 n2 adr len -- n3 -1 | 0 )                          cr ." Enter"  type  ." : "  enter  cr  dup if                     number? if                                                        d>s  dup 2swap between  ?dup and                              end                                                           then  2nip nip ;                                                                                                              : SELECT ( n1 n2 -- n3 -1 | 0 )  s" "  #select ;                                                                                : ANYKEY ( -- )  cr ." Press any key to continue "  key drop ;                                                                  : INVALID ( -- )  cr ." Invalid or nothing entered" cr ;                                                                                                                                        \ CPU-SPEED                                                     \ Edit CPU speed                                                : CPU-SPEED ( -- )                                                cls  ." CPU speed is "                                          $124 >target  dup @ u. ." MHz "  change? if                       1 8191  s"  (1-8191)"  #select if                                 over !                                                        else  invalid  then  anykey                                   then  drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ CHG-DELAY DELAY-TIMES                                         \ Change delay specified by adr & string                        : CHG-DELAY ( a adr len -- )                                      cr cr  type ."  delay "                                         >target  dup c@ . ." mS "  change? if                             0 255  s"  (0-255)"  #select if                                   over c!                                                       else  invalid  then  anykey                                   then  drop ;                                                                                                                  \ Change delay times                                            : DELAY-TIMES ( -- )  cls                                         $1A0  s" Cursor Motion"  chg-delay                              $1BA  s" Clear Screen"  chg-delay                               $1CE  s" Clear to End-of-Line"  chg-delay ;                                                                                   \ >BUF @STR !STR @BYT !BYT                                      \ Convert offset to adr in terminal buffer                      : >BUF ( n -- a )  tbuf + ;                                                                                                     : @STR ( ofs -- a u )  >buf count ;                             : !STR ( a u ofs -- )  >buf place ;                             : @BYT ( ofs -- c )    >buf c@ ;                                : !BYT ( c ofs -- )    >buf c! ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ <BS> <CR> VISIBLE? .CHR                                       8 constant <BS>   13 constant <CR>                                                                                              : VISIBLE? ( c -- flag )  bl 127 within ;                                                                                       : .CHR ( c -- )                                                   cond                                                              10  of ." <LF>"    else  <cr> of ." <CR>"   else                27  of ." <ESC>"   else  bl   of ." <SP>"   else                127 of ." <DEL>"   else                                         dup bl <         if  ." Ctrl-"  [char] @ +    else              dup visible? not if  [char] $ emit  .hb  end  then  emit      cont  space ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ .DEC .STR #DIGIT /FIELD                                       : .DEC ( adr len -- )                                             ."  ("  begin  dup while  over c@ 0 .r  1 /string               dup while  space  repeat then  2drop  ." ) " ;                                                                                : .STR ( offs -- )                                                @str  dup if                                                      2dup  bounds ?do  i c@ .chr  loop  .dec                       end  2drop  ." <none> " ;                                                                                                     variable #DIGIT  \ #digits entered                                                                                              : /FIELD ( -- )                                                   #digit @  begin  dup while                                        <bs> emit  space  <bs> emit  1-                               repeat  #digit ! ;                                            \ >DIGIT +DIGIT BUILD#                                          : >DIGIT ( c -- u flag )                                          [char] 0 -  dup 10 16 between  or                               dup 16 >  7 and  -  dup base @ u< ;                                                                                           : +DIGIT ( u c -- u' err )                                        >digit if  swap base @ * +  dup 255 u>  end  drop true ;                                                                      : BUILD# ( c -- n c2 )  \ CR or BL exits                          decimal  #digit off  0 swap  begin                                [char] $ of ." $"  hex  key  then  upcase                       dup bl <>  over <cr> <>  and while                              dup visible? if  dup emit  1 #digit +!  then                    +digit if  beep  /field  drop 0  then  key                    repeat  decimal ;                                                                                                             \ GET# LEN MAXCHR ROOM? +CHR DO-NUM                             : GET# ( -- n )  key build# drop ;                                                                                              variable LEN   0 value MAXCHR                                                                                                   : ROOM? ( -- f )  len @  maxchr <  ;                                                                                            : +CHR ( c -- )  ibuf len @ +  c!  1 len +! ;                                                                                   : DO-NUM ( c -- )                                                 begin  room? while                                                build#  swap  #digit @ if  +chr  else  drop  then               <cr> = if end  space  key                                     repeat  drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                \ DO-ASC NUM? GET$                                              : DO-ASC ( c -- )                                                 begin  dup <cr> -  room?  and while                               dup .chr  +chr  key                                           repeat  drop ;                                                                                                                : DIGIT? ( c -- f )                                               dup [char] $ =  swap [char] 0 [char] 9 between  or ;                                                                          : GET$ ( maxlen -- adr len )                                      to maxchr  len off                                              key  dup digit? if  do-num  else  do-asc  then                  ibuf len @ ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ SET$ SET# SETF !FLAG                                          : SET$ ( ofs size -- )                                            over .str  change?                                              if  cr ." : "  get$  rot !str  end  2drop ;                                                                                   : SET# ( ofs -- )                                                 dup @byt .  change? if ." : "  get#  swap !byt  end  drop ;                                                                   : SETF ( ofs -- 0|1 )                                             dup @byt  dup .yn  change? if  0= 1 and  then  dup rot !byt ;                                                                 \ Set offset2 flag according to string offset1                  : !FLAG ( ofs1 ofs2 -- )  >r  @byt  0<> 1 and  r> !byt ;                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ ?NAME ?INIT ?RESET                                            : ?NAME ( -- )                                                    0 0  begin                                                        2drop                                                           cr ." Terminal type: "  0 @str type  space                      isiz  dup [char] _ emits  <bs> emits                            enter  dup  0 @byt  or                                        until  tbuf ?place ;                                                                                                          : ?INIT ( -- )                                                    cr ." Term INIT string: "  $16  dup 15 set$  $7D !flag ;                                                                      : ?RESET ( -- )                                                   cr ." Term RESET string: "  $26  dup 15 set$  $7E !flag ;                                                                                                                                     \ ?LEADIN ?BETWEEN ?AFTER ?COLFIRST ?ROFS ?COFS                 : ?LEADIN ( -- )                                                  cr ." CURSOR LEAD-IN command: "  $80 5 set$ ;                                                                                 : ?BETWEEN ( -- )                                                 cr ." CURSOR command BETWEEN row/col: "  $86 5 set$ ;                                                                         : ?AFTER ( -- )                                                   cr ." CURSOR command AFTER row/col: "  $8C 5 set$ ;                                                                           : ?COLFIRST ( -- )                                                cr ." Column first? "  $92 setf drop ;                                                                                        : ?ROFS ( -- )  cr ." OFFSET to add to ROW: "  $4A set# ;                                                                       : ?COFS ( -- )  cr ." OFFSET to add to COL: "  $49 set# ;       \ ?DIGITS ?BINARY ?CLS                                          : ?DIGITS ( -- n )                                                cr ." ASCII digits (2 or 3): "                                  $93 @byt  dup .  change?  0= if end  ." : "                     begin  drop  key  [char] 0 -  dup 2 3 between not               while  beep  repeat  dup . ;                                                                                                  : ?BINARY ( -- )                                                  cr ." Binary address? "  $46 setf                               0 of  ?digits  then  $93 !byt ;                                                                                               : ?CLS ( -- )  cr ." CLEAR SCREEN command: "  $4D 5 set$ ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ ?HOM ?DEL ?INS ?EOL ?BOLD                                     : ?HOM ( -- )                                                     cr ." Does CLEAR SCREEN also HOME cursor? "                     $53  dup @byt  dup not .yn  change?  over 0<> xor if              drop  cr ." HOME command: "  5 set$                           end  if  0 over !byt  then  drop ;                                                                                            : ?DEL ( -- )  cr ." DELETE LINE command: "  $75 5 set$ ;                                                                       : ?INS ( -- )  cr ." INSERT LINE command: "  $6F 5 set$ ;                                                                       : ?EOL ( -- )  cr ." ERASE TO EOL command: "  $69 5 set$ ;                                                                      : ?BOLD ( -- )  cr ." BOLD VIDEO command: "  $5B 5 set$ ;                                                                                                                                       \ ?NORM ?ROWS ?COLS ?DCUR ?DCLS ?DEOL                           : ?NORM ( -- )  cr ." NORMAL VIDEO command: "  $61 5 set$ ;                                                                     : ?ROWS ( -- )  cr ." Number of screen rows: "  $7C set# ;                                                                      : ?COLS ( -- )  cr ." Number of screen cols: "  $7B set# ;                                                                      : ?DCUR ( -- )                                                    cr ." Delay after CURSOR ADDRESS: "  $4B set# ;                                                                               : ?DCLS ( -- )                                                    cr ." Delay after CLEAR, DELETE, INSERT: "  $59 set# ;                                                                        : ?DEOL ( -- )                                                    cr ." Delay after ERASE-EOL, BOLD, NORMAL: "  $67 set# ;                                                                      \ CMT #CMT BIN? CO? #DIG RC$ !RCOFS                             : CMT  ( -- a )    $36 >buf ;  \ cursor motion template         : #CMT ( -- ofs )  $36 @byt ;  \ current size/offset            : BIN? ( -- f )    $46 @byt ;  \ binary?                        : COL? ( -- f )    $92 @byt ;  \ column first?                  : #DIG ( -- n )    $93 @byt ;  \ #digits for row/col                                                                            \ Row/col string                                                : RC$ ( -- a n )                                                  bin? if  [ pad dup off 1 ] sliteral  end                        s" 000" drop #dig ;                                                                                                           \ Store template offsets                                        : !RCOFS ( cofs rofs -- )                                         col? if  swap  then  $47 !byt  $48 !byt ;                                                                                     \ !CMT MODIFY                                                   : !CMT ( -- )  \ init cursor motion template                      $80 @str  cmt  place          \ lead-in                         rc$       cmt +place   #cmt   \ col, offs                       $86 @str  cmt +place          \ between                         rc$       cmt +place   #cmt   \ row, offs                       $8C @str  cmt +place          \ after                           !rcofs ;                      \ row/col offsets                                                                               \ Modify terminal definition in temp buffer                     : MODIFY ( -- )  cls                                              ?name ?init ?reset ?leadin ?between ?after ?colfirst            ?rofs ?cofs ?binary ?cls ?hom ?del ?ins ?eol                    ?bold ?norm ?rows ?cols ?dcur ?dcls ?deol                       !cmt                                                            0 $94 !byt ;                  \ TINST always clears?          \ +TERM GET-TERM INS-TERM                                       \ Bump #terms & update DTA header                               : +TERM ( n -- )                                                   #terms +  dup to #terms  dta-base !                             catalog  altered on ;                                                                                                        : GET-TERM ( -- )  \ copy term in DTA to buffer                   dbuf tbuf tlen cmove ;                                                                                                        \ Insert a terminal                                             : INS-TERM ( -- )                                                 tbuf dta-end tlen cmove  1 +term ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ SAVE-MOD? INIT-TERM ?NEW-TERM                                 : SAVE-MOD? ( -- f )                                              cr ." Save modifications? "  y/n ;                                                                                            : INIT-TERM ( -- )                                                tbuf tlen erase                                                 1  $46 !byt  1  $92 !byt     \ binary, column first             24 $7C !byt  80 $7B !byt ;   \ #rows, #columns                                                                                : ?NEW-TERM ( -- )                                                cr ." New definition? "  y/n  0= if end                         init-term  modify  save-mod? if  ins-term  then ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \ DEL-TERM ?DELETE                                              \ Delete selected terminal                                      : DEL-TERM ( -- )                                                 dbuf tlen +  dta-end over -  dbuf swap cmove                    -1 +term ;                                                                                                                    : ?DELETE ( -- )                                                  #terms 0= if  cr ." Nothing to delete" cr  end                  cr ." Enter terminal # to delete" cr                            1 #terms select if ( delete)                                      1-  dup to term  name  cr type                                  ."   Are you sure? "  y/n if  del-term  then  cr              end  invalid ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ ?MODIFY !TERM !ZTCAP                                          \ Modify selected terminal                                      : ?MODIFY ( -- )                                                  cr ." Modify definition? "  y/n  0= if end                      get-term  modify  save-mod? if  del-term  ins-term  then ;                                                                    \ Install selected terminal                                     : !TERM ( -- )                                                    ?modify                                                         tname tinit texit tcm tbin tpos toffs tdcm tcls thom            tdcls thil tnor tdeol teol tins tdel tcr cpu-speed ;                                                                          \ Install from Z-System TCAP                                    : !ZTCAP ( -- )  zenv if  zinstall  cpu-speed  end                cr ." Z-System not present" cr  anykey  unnest unnest ;                                                                       \ DO-TERM #LINES VALID? ?SPACES .LINE                           : DO-TERM ( -- )                                                  term                                                            #terms    of  !ztcap     end                                    #terms 1+ of  ?new-term  end                                    #terms 2+ of  ?delete    end                                    drop  !term ;                                                                                                                 10 constant #LINES  \ lines to display                                                                                          : VALID? ( n -- n f )  dup #terms 1+ < ;                                                                                        : ?SPACES ( -- )  out @  ?dup if  25 swap - spaces  then ;                                                                      : .LINE ( n adr len -- )  ?spaces  rot 1+  3 .r  space type ;                                                                   \ .TERM .TERMS .OPTIONS                                         : .TERM ( n -- )                                                  dup #terms < if  dup name .line  end                            dup #terms = if  s" Z-System Termcap" .line  end                drop ;                                                                                                                        : .TERMS ( n -- )  \ one page of terminals                        cr  #lines 0 do                                                   valid? if  cr  then                                             dup .term  dup #lines + .term  1+                             loop drop  cr ;                                                                                                               : .OPTIONS ( -- )  cr                                             #terms 1+  s" None of the above"    .line                       #terms 2+  s" Delete a definition"  .line  cr ;                                                                               \ SEL-TERM                                                      \ Display terminals and select                                  : SEL-TERM ( -- )                                                 cls  0  begin                                                     dup .terms  .options                                            1 #terms 3 + select if ( exec)                                    1- to term  drop  do-term  cr                                 end                                                             invalid  cr ." ESC to exit, other key for more "                key  27 ( Esc) -                                              while                                                             #lines 2* +  valid? and  \ looping                            repeat drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ CHANGE-TERM                                                   : CHANGE-TERM ( -- )                                              cls  ." Terminal is: "                                          $153 >target count  -trailing type                              change? if                                                        sel-term                                                      then ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        \ CHG-KEY                                                       \ Change key specified by adr & string                          : CHG-KEY ( a adr len -- )                                        cr cr  type ."  code "                                          >target  dup c@  [char] $ emit  .hb  change? if                   cr ." Enter new value in hex"                                   0 $FF  s"  (00-FF)"  hex #select decimal  if                      over c!                                                       else  invalid  then  anykey                                   then  drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ KEY-CODES                                                     \ Change key codes                                              : KEY-CODES ( -- )                                                cls  ." Use default backspace & arrow keys? "  y/n if             $08         $14E >target c!                                     $18051304.  $14F >target 2!                                   end                                                             $14E  s" BACKSPACE"    chg-key                                  $14F  s" UP    arrow"  chg-key                                  $150  s" DOWN  arrow"  chg-key                                  $151  s" RIGHT arrow"  chg-key                                  $152  s" LEFT  arrow"  chg-key                                ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \ NOBOOT                                                        \ Change the warmboot option                                    : NOBOOT ( -- )                                                   cls  ." NO WARMBOOT is "                                        $110 >target ( a)  dup c@ .onoff                                change? if                                                        dup c@  not  over c!  cr  anykey                              then  drop ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ SAVE-SETUP .MENU                                              \ Save to disk and exit                                         : SAVE-SETUP ( -- )                                               beep  cr ." Save current setup to disk? "  y/n if                 save-target  save-dta  unnest ( exit menu loop)               then ;                                                                                                                        \ Display main menu                                             : .MENU ( -- )                                                    cr ."    1. Terminal selection"                                 cr ."    2. CPU speed"                                          cr ."    3. Time delays"                                        cr ."    4. Key codes"                                          cr ."    5. No Warmboot"                                        cr ."    6. Save changes and exit" ;                                                                                          \ MENU                                                          \ Main menu loop. Exit if invalid option or nothing entered.    : MENU ( -- )                                                     begin  .menu cr  1 6 select while                                 cond  1 of  change-term  else                                         2 of  cpu-speed    else                                         3 of  delay-times  else                                         4 of  key-codes    else                                         5 of  noboot       else                                         6 of  save-setup   else                                         drop                                                      cont  cls                                                     repeat ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      \ INIT INSTALL                                                  : INIT ( -- )                                                     altered off                 \ clear                             isiz       reserve to ibuf  \ console input                     tlen       reserve to tbuf  \ temp terminal buffer              chunk      reserve to sbuf  \ swap/work buffer                  tmax cells reserve to xbuf  \ terminal index                  ;                                                                                                                               \ Main                                                          : INSTALL ( -- )                                                  cls title  init                                                 open-target  read-dta  catalog                                  menu                                                            close-target                                                  ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               